  "state": "same task (same system and user prompt) and the same sequence of executed tool actions with the same observed tool outputs before the decision. Free-text reasoning (assistant prose and `think` calls) is excluded: it differs between every run and does not change the workspace. Two matching levels reported: exact outputs, and normalised outputs (ANSI codes, timings, memory addresses, temp paths, timestamps and whitespace normalised). Three levels, never combined: (1) EXACT observed-history matches = the headline; (2) NORMALISED matches = exploratory; (3) verified identical WORKSPACE states = 0 available: the dataset has no workspace snapshots, so no branch is a verified identical environment (same calls and outputs can still hide different unobserved file contents). Task instructions (system and user prompt) are part of every state",
  "action": "a tool call (name + canonical JSON arguments without is_input / timeout / security_risk / thought; bash commands whitespace-collapsed). Branchpoint: a state reached by >= 2 runs whose next actions are >= 2 different actions",
  "action_types": "read (editor view; cat / head / tail / sed -n / less / nl), search (grep / rg / find / ls / tree), test (pytest / unittest / tox / test scripts), run (other python / node / go / make / script execution), edit (editor create / str_replace / insert / undo; sed -i, redirections, patch), vcs (git), env (pip / apt / npm install / conda), stop (finish), plan (task_tracker), other",
  "outcome": "each child action's runs and their final `resolved` flags: OBSERVATIONAL evidence (later steps also matter), never a verified label",
  "evidence tiers": {
   "single": ">= 2 children with different resolve rates (any run counts)",
   "repeated": ">= 2 children with >= 2 runs each and different resolve rates",
   "strong": ">= 2 children with >= 3 runs each and resolve rates differing by >= 0.3"
  },
  "initial_vs_later": "depth 0 (the first executed action after the task prompt) vs depth >= 1",
  "independence": "unique tasks, repos and trajectories counted at every funnel stage; branchpoints inside one task are not independent",
  "overlap": "858 = size of the source-side repo list (coding-decision-cases, nebius/SWE-agent rows); 618 = its recorded overlap with the full nebius set; the filtered 859 repos are checked against the list here. Overlap is a contamination RISK, not proof an example was in pretraining",
  "stage1_gate": ">= 95% of runs parse and >= 95% of tool calls are matched to a tool output, on the first 50 tasks (sorted by instance id)",
  "discovery_threshold": "EXACT matches: >= 300 branchpoints with >= 2 action TYPES and single-tier outcome evidence, from >= 100 repos (not a training gate)"
